<title>PORTUGAL: FORECAST - Portugal spreads vs Bunds, Spanish Bonos.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Portugal spreads vs Bunds, Spanish Bonos.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the daily forecast for spreads in the Portuguese bond market based on a poll of four banks and one brokerage.</p>
<p>Poll covers spreads between the February 2007 Portuguese cash bond (OT) and the German and Spanish equivalents, together with the spreads between the Portuguese 10 and two-year bonds.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>			     Min spread Avge  Max  vs previous close</p>
<p>Feb 07 vs Bund July  07   67 bps   70   74	     71</p>
<p>Feb 07 vs Bono March 07    -1     -1.4  -3	     -1</p>
<p>						  YLDS3</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>				 Min  Avge   Max</p>
<p>Feb 07 vs March 99	 100  111.8  116     vs     109.8</p>
<p>						  PT/CURVE</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Key factors likely to affect market:</p>
<p>- Strength of other periphery markets, buoyed by hopes for an accord on the European Union's Stability Pact, should lift the longer end. But spread with Bund not seen narrowing, nor will the yield curve steepen.</p>
<p>--Sergio Goncalves, Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
